\pard\li0\sb120\sa120\keepn\outlinelevel0 {\b\fs35 GetMssgPatCopies}\par
\pard\li0\sb0\sa120 {GetMssgPatCopies looks in a folder of patent copies for the ones that are {\b zero bytes} in size (the copies that did not come through) and writes their numbers into two files in that same folder, so they can be fetched again:}\par
\trowd\trgaph80\trleft-80\trhdr\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\clcbpat3\clvertalt\cellx2617\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\clcbpat3\clvertalt\cellx9279\pard\intbl\ql\sb0\sa0 {\fs20 \b File}\cell\pard\intbl\ql\sb0\sa0 {\fs20 \b Contents}\cell\row
\trowd\trgaph80\trleft-80\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\clvertalt\cellx2617\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\clvertalt\cellx9279\pard\intbl\ql\sb0\sa0 {\fs20 {\f1\fs20 MssgPat-Order.txt}}\cell\pard\intbl\ql\sb0\sa0 {\fs20 Fetcher Format: one number per line, Windows line endings, in the standard form PatCopyPrint uses ({\f1\fs20 01234567}, {\f1\fs20 20120001234}, {\f1\fs20 D0512345})}\cell\row
\trowd\trgaph80\trleft-80\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\clvertalt\cellx2617\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\clvertalt\cellx9279\pard\intbl\ql\sb0\sa0 {\fs20 {\f1\fs20 MssgPat-USPTO-Order.txt}}\cell\pard\intbl\ql\sb0\sa0 {\fs20 One line to paste into the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ppubs.uspto.gov/pubwebapp/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2\ul USPTO Patent Public Search}}} box: {\f1\fs20 ("1234567" or "20120001234" or "D512345").pn.} (a list too long for one search is split into several lines, one search each; see The USPTO search)}\cell\row
\pard\li0\sb0\sa100 {\fs2 }\par
\pard\li0\sb0\sa120 {Both lists are in the same order, the sorted order of PatCopyPrint and RemoveDupNumbers: patents by number, then published applications by number, then D, H, PP, RE and the other letter prefixes.}\par
\pard\li0\sb0\sa120 {{\i The GetMssgPatCopies window after Generate}}\par
\pard\li0\sb0\sa120 {It is one Python program, {\f1\fs20 GetMssgPatCopies.py}, that runs anywhere PatCopyPrint runs (Windows 7, Windows 11, Ubuntu 14.10 with Python 3.4, Fedora) and needs only Python's own library. It opens a window when tkinter is available and otherwise works in the terminal. Nothing is sent anywhere.}\par
\pard\li0\sb240\sa120\keepn\outlinelevel1 {\b\fs29 Starting it}\par
\pard\li360\sb0\sa40\fi-360\tx360 {\bullet\tab {\b Windows:} put {\f1\fs20 GetMssgPatCopies.py} and {\f1\fs20 GetMssgPatCopies.pyw} in the same folder and double-click {\b {\f1\fs20 GetMssgPatCopies.pyw}} (no black console window).}\par
\pard\li360\sb0\sa40\fi-360\tx360 {\bullet\tab {\b Linux:} {\f1\fs20 python3 GetMssgPatCopies.py}.}\par
\pard\li360\sb0\sa120\fi-360\tx360 {\bullet\tab {\f1\fs20 python3 GetMssgPatCopies.py --console} uses the terminal even when a window is possible, and {\f1\fs20 python3 GetMssgPatCopies.py FOLDER --yes} writes the two files for FOLDER without asking anything.}\par
\pard\li0\sb0\sa120 {Installing Python (also offline) is described in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/Al-bit-dot/PatCopyPrint#installing-python-on-a-computer-with-no-internet"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2\ul PatCopyPrint README}}}; GetMssgPatCopies needs the same Python and nothing more.}\par
\pard\li0\sb0\sa120 {The last folder is remembered in {\f1\fs20 .getmssgpatcopies.json} in your home folder.}\par
\pard\li0\sb240\sa120\keepn\outlinelevel1 {\b\fs29 Using the window}\par
\pard\li360\sb0\sa40\fi-360\tx360 {1.\tab Pick the folder as in PatCopyPrint: {\b Choose folder\u8230\'85} opens one, and the list shows its sub-folders (in blue) and its files with their sizes. Click a folder line or {\f1\fs20 ..} to move around. The folder whose contents are shown is the one that will be read. Zero-byte patent copies are shown in red.}\par
\pard\li360\sb0\sa40\fi-360\tx360 {2.\tab Click {\b Generate}. If the two files are already in the folder you are asked once before they are replaced. The result is shown below the button with the numbers found and the USPTO search.}\par
\pard\li360\sb0\sa120\fi-360\tx360 {3.\tab {\b Copy USPTO search} puts the USPTO search on the clipboard. On the Patent Public Search page close the {\i Notification} pop-up, paste it into the search box and click {\b Search}. When the search has been split, the button reads {\b Copy USPTO search 1 of 3}; each click copies the next one.}\par
\pard\li0\sb240\sa120\keepn\outlinelevel1 {\b\fs29 Using the terminal}\par
\pard\li0\sb0\sa120 {The program lists the sub-folders of the remembered folder. Type a number to open a folder, a path to go somewhere else, {\f1\fs20 g} (or just Enter) to generate the files for the folder shown, or {\f1\fs20 q} to quit.}\par
\pard\li0\sb240\sa120\keepn\outlinelevel1 {\b\fs29 Which files count}\par
\pard\li0\sb0\sa120 {Only the files directly in the chosen folder are read (not its sub-folders). A file counts as a patent copy when its name without the extension is a US number in any of these spellings:}\par
\trowd\trgaph80\trleft-80\trhdr\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\clcbpat3\clvertalt\cellx1618\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\clcbpat3\clvertalt\cellx6174\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\clcbpat3\clvertalt\cellx7652\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\clcbpat3\clvertalt\cellx9277\pard\intbl\ql\sb0\sa0 {\fs20 \b Kind}\cell\pard\intbl\ql\sb0\sa0 {\fs20 \b File names recognised}\cell\pard\intbl\ql\sb0\sa0 {\fs20 \b Fetcher list}\cell\pard\intbl\ql\sb0\sa0 {\fs20 \b USPTO line}\cell\row
